# Checkpoint 6 - the stale-geometry test. Run this, then c6-single-a and
# c6-single-b as separate processes, and compare.
# This is the one test that justifies letting geometry move after
# /run/initialize. If GeometryHasBeenModified() were ineffective, the second run
# would transport through the theta=0 world while reporting theta=30 - a
# projection that looks plausible and is wrong.
# Seeds reset to the SAME value before each beamOn so the comparison is exact:
#     batched run 1 == c6-single-a   (bit for bit)
#     batched run 2 == c6-single-b   (bit for bit)
# If equality holds only within statistics under MT, re-run all three with
# /run/numberOfThreads 1 before /run/initialize.
/run/verbose      0
/event/verbose    0
/tracking/verbose 0
/cttwin/phantom bars
/run/initialize
/cttwin/scan/translation 0 mm
/random/setSeeds 12345 67890
/cttwin/scan/angle  0 deg
/run/beamOn 100000
/random/setSeeds 12345 67890
/cttwin/scan/angle 30 deg
/run/beamOn 100000
